{#
    `.. glossary::` — the words a project defines, and where they are defined.

    The core writes the definition list into a div and stops, so a page can
    name forty terms and point at none of them. Each term gets the id its own
    words make and the mark a heading carries, which is the whole difference
    between a list of definitions and a glossary a sentence elsewhere can link
    into.

    Rebuilt rather than handed to `renderNode`, because the id belongs on the
    `<dt>` and nothing else can put it there. A body that holds no terms — a
    paragraph, a nested directive — falls back to the core's rendering rather
    than coming out empty.
#}
{%- set entries = terms(node.value) -%}
{%- if entries is empty -%}
    {{ renderNode(node.value) }}
{%- else -%}
<dl>
    {%- for entry in entries -%}
        {%- set anchor = entry.term.toString|anchor -%}
        <dt id="{{ anchor }}">
            {{- renderNode(entry.term) -}}
            {%- for classifier in entry.classifiers %} <span class="classifier-delimiter">:</span>
                <span class="classifier">{{- renderNode(classifier) -}}</span>
            {%- endfor -%}
            <a class="sds-permalink" href="#{{ anchor }}" aria-label="Permalink to {{ entry.term.toString }}">#</a>
        </dt>
        {%- for definition in entry.children -%}
            <dd>{{- renderNode(definition) -}}</dd>
        {%- endfor -%}
    {%- endfor %}
</dl>
{%- endif -%}
